WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:21.272
The Little Mermaid felt the warmth of the morning sun on her face.

2
00:00:21.273 --> 00:00:27.049
To her surprise she was not dead and had not turned into sea foam.

3
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.202
Instead she was floating above the water.

4
00:00:31.203 --> 00:00:36.597
"It is dawn and I am still alive?" she wondered.

5
00:00:36.598 --> 00:00:42.278
Above her head were two strange beings in long, white robes.

6
00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:45.450
They looked as if they were waiting to greet her.

7
00:00:45.451 --> 00:00:49.569
They smiled as they floated in the air like clouds.

8
00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:54.580
She tried to touch them, but her hand went right through them.

9
00:00:54.581 --> 00:00:59.835
The Little Mermaid soon discovered that she was dressed in a robe too.

10
00:00:59.836 --> 00:01:05.805
Like them she was also part of the air and floating like a cloud.

11
00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:10.901
Without thinking she called out to them, "Who are you?"

12
00:01:10.902 --> 00:01:15.182
To her surprise she heard her own voice.

13
00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:20.770
And it was just as beautiful as it had been before she gave it to the Sea Witch.

14
00:01:20.771 --> 00:01:25.686
"We are the Spirits of the Air," one of them replied.

15
00:01:25.687 --> 00:01:29.704
"We travel through the world doing good deeds."

16
00:01:29.705 --> 00:01:33.909
"Why am I here with you?" the Little Mermaid asked.

17
00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:43.645
"Your loyalty to the Prince and your sacrifice has raised you up to the world of Air Spirits," the other said.

18
00:01:43.646 --> 00:01:46.653
"You are now one of us."

19
00:01:46.654 --> 00:01:49.158
The mermaid was curious.

20
00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:50.761
"I need to know more.

21
00:01:50.762 --> 00:01:54.375
Do you live for three hundred years like the sea folk?

22
00:01:54.376 --> 00:01:57.403
Do you have a soul like the humans?"

23
00:01:57.404 --> 00:02:03.123
"Here, in our world, we also live for three hundred years.

24
00:02:03.124 --> 00:02:05.510
But we can earn our souls.

25
00:02:05.511 --> 00:02:09.480
When we do, we live forever."

26
00:02:09.481 --> 00:02:13.861
"I've always wanted a soul," said the mermaid.

27
00:02:13.862 --> 00:02:16.727
"What must I do to deserve one?"

28
00:02:16.728 --> 00:02:26.331
"If you do many good deeds throughout your three hundred years, you will get a soul," answered one of the air spirits.

29
00:02:26.332 --> 00:02:28.863
"Exactly what is a good deed?"

30
00:02:28.864 --> 00:02:33.034
asked the Little Mermaid, now very interested.

31
00:02:33.035 --> 00:02:37.631
"A good deed is when you do something nice for humans.

32
00:02:37.632 --> 00:02:41.553
The Spirits of the Air watch over humans.

33
00:02:41.554 --> 00:02:46.887
We bring them food when they are hungry and clothes when they are cold.

34
00:02:46.888 --> 00:02:52.477
Sometimes we whisper good thoughts into their ears when they are sad.

35
00:02:52.478 --> 00:02:56.570
We try to help in any way we can."

36
00:02:56.571 --> 00:03:00.844
Pleased, the Little Mermaid looked down to the earth.

37
00:03:00.845 --> 00:03:06.062
She liked the idea of watching over the humans, whom she had learned to love.

38
00:03:06.063 --> 00:03:12.885
"I finally have a chance to earn a soul," she said, laughing.

39
00:03:12.886 --> 00:03:19.745
The Little Mermaid's joy was so great that, for the first time in her life, she began to cry.

40
00:03:19.746 --> 00:03:25.200
Her tears of happiness fell one by one into the sea below her.

41
00:03:25.201 --> 00:03:29.190
Then the Little Mermaid saw the grand ship.

42
00:03:29.191 --> 00:03:33.266
She could see that everyone on board was now awake.

43
00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:37.844
The Prince and his bride were looking for her and calling out.

44
00:03:37.845 --> 00:03:43.375
After a while they just gazed sadly out to sea.

45
00:03:43.376 --> 00:03:47.913
"What has happened to my little companion?" wondered the Prince.

46
00:03:47.914 --> 00:03:50.602
"She was so faithful to me."

47
00:03:50.603 --> 00:03:55.903
The Little Mermaid blew him a kiss that turned into a white feather.

48
00:03:55.904 --> 00:04:00.630
Floating softly down, it brushed the Prince's cheek.

49
00:04:00.631 --> 00:04:04.116
Then she blew another kiss to his bride.

50
00:04:04.117 --> 00:04:15.463
She wished them both well—her first good deed.
